⚠ READ THIS FIRST, BEFORE INSTALLING

**The Android build has not run since the React 18 -> 19 upgrade, and it would
have FAILED if it had.** Every clean install died at the first step:

    npm error code ERESOLVE
    npm error While resolving: react-day-picker@8.10.1
    npm error Found: react@19.2.8

`npm ci` is the first line of this workflow, so this build is ALSO the first
proof that the fix (`.npmrc`, `legacy-peer-deps=true`) works here. If the job
fails at "Install dependencies", that is why, and the log will say so plainly.

The same breakage stopped the WEBSITE deploying for nine hours today, through a
second stale lockfile: Cloudflare Pages installs with `bun`, and `bun.lock`
still pinned React 18. Both lockfiles are now correct and the website is live
and verified.

WHAT IS IN THIS BUILD

THE UPLOAD COMPOSER, rebuilt
- A true preview at the frame the post will actually get, `object-contain`, so
  nothing is cropped away silently.
- A rule-of-thirds guide over it. Decoration only: not in the upload, not in
  the tab order, invisible to a screen reader.
- Reorder by arrows, a "Cover" badge on the first photo, an n/N counter.
- The remove button no longer overlaps the NEXT thumbnail. Its 44px target used
  to hang over its neighbour, so tapping one photo's left edge deleted the photo
  before it. Unrecoverable in a composer.
- A photo that will not preview says so, instead of leaving a hole with
  Chromium's own torn-page glyph in the corner.

THE POST CARD
- Reach and Viewed moved OFF the action row and onto the photograph: hover on
  web, FIRST TAP in the app (second tap opens the photo, as always). They are
  computed after the card paints, so in the row they made it reflow under your
  thumb - that is the "reactions shifting" you reported.
- The right of the row now carries each reaction with its own count, Facebook
  style; the total stays on the left beside the thumb.
- A caption that is one long word (a filename, a pasted url) no longer runs off
  the card and gets sliced mid-word.

THE WALL
- Deleting a post fades it out. That animation never ran: it was keyed on a
  Fragment, which cannot hold the reference the animation needs, and React
  logged an error for every post on every render.

WHAT TO CHECK ON THE PHONE - only your device can answer these

  1. Post a photo. Reorder it, crop it, remove one. The preview must match what
     is published.
  2. Tap a photo in the feed ONCE: the reach/viewed chip appears and NOTHING
     opens. Tap again: it opens.
  3. Double-tap a photo: it likes, and the viewer does NOT open.
  4. Delete one of your own posts on your wall: it fades, it does not vanish.
  5. Scroll the feed hard and back: no blank cards, no jump, no row shifting
     under your thumb as you reach for it.
  6. A post with a very long one-word caption: "See more" appears, nothing is
     cut off at the edge.

